{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06UH", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-existence-residual-gerbes}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:93f43a4f31d398d7f8404e29123faaf416a36ac24cbba91ae9f529fe846798f4", "source_text": "Existence of residual gerbes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:92994aeb09eca0b599e2f4e60a3423cfbf1be86fe1cb8dc18c64a3673c5f56f1", "unit_id": "tag:06UH:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06UH", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-definition-residual-gerbe}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-point-finite-type-monomorphism}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-residual-gerbe-exists}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{proposition-open-stratum}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01f7c7009b6bf7394e71b92377041917530c293d9e0ebe67416920cf1c6a895c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe definition of a residual gerbe of a point on an algebraic stack\nis Properties of Stacks, Definition\n<REF_0001>.\nWe have already shown that residual gerbes exist for finite type\npoints (Lemma <REF_0002>)\nand for any point of a gerbe (Lemma <REF_0003>).\nIn this section we prove that residual gerbes\nexist on many algebraic stacks. First, here is the promised\napplication of\nProposition <REF_0004>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c0a9cd60e3431c68165e407c5527237c44bcb3a90fb518a1708c5bdeb5ef83ca", "unit_id": "tag:06UH:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06UH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-every-point-residual-gerbe}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:479d29c3c6d5950d3854d3f55743e34470998405e089ca907f13c7da7a58493a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6915755904e9396cb8dbb08f492429086adbd3f6a558b1db8d14213ceb34992b", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack such that\n<MATH_0002> is quasi-compact.\nThen the residual gerbe of <MATH_0003> at <MATH_0004> exists for\nevery <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eb4f00c545fbd6663372a22e5f6d1bb4a14fd25b37184bcb4d44956a467a664f", "unit_id": "tag:06RD:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06UH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T = \\overline{\\{x\\}} \\subset |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X}' \\subset \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$T = |\\mathcal{X}'|$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{X}'} =\n\\mathcal{I}_\\mathcal{X} \\times_\\mathcal{X} \\mathcal{X}'$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I}_{\\mathcal{X}'} \\to \\mathcal{X}'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{U} \\subset \\mathcal{X}'$", "MATH_0008": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{U}|$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{x\\} \\subset T$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x \\subset \\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0012": "$x$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{Z}_x \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0015": "$x$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-lemma-reduced-closed-substack}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-monomorphism-cartesian-square-inertia}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-quasi-compact}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{proposition-open-stratum}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-gerbe-residual-gerbe-exists}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:442f2c74339061130226aac92340fcd2417b858c66610f89e6b0da77cc22c0c0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dac64a1848e8d484f7a1f90e3dc28a7c0469e677188b81374fde3787764998df", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be the closure of <MATH_0002>.\nBy\nProperties of Stacks, Lemma\n<REF_0001>\nthere exists a reduced closed substack <MATH_0003>\nsuch that <MATH_0004>. Note that\n<MATH_0005> by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nHence <MATH_0006> is\nquasi-compact as a base change, see\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nTherefore\nProposition <REF_0004>\nimplies there exists a dense open substack\n<MATH_0007>\nwhich is a gerbe. Note that <MATH_0008> because <MATH_0009>\nis a dense subset too. Hence a residual gerbe\n<MATH_0010> of <MATH_0011> at <MATH_0012> exists by\nLemma <REF_0005>.\nIt is immediate from the definitions that <MATH_0013>\nis a residual gerbe of <MATH_0014> at <MATH_0015>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:00bc970359a6f4002700da6314f092dd95ffea32e8d725eeab5f47d960b0de8e", "unit_id": "tag:06RD:proof"}
